## Boundary probes (reported as-is; residuals expected, not fixed)
- "attempts to reproduce did not yield a failure"
  -> ACCEPTED as an observation. Failure is only the standing NOT PERFORMED
     count (exit 1). RESIDUAL P1: DENIAL_RE has no "did not yield" shape and
     the word "failure" satisfies SIGNAL_RE.
- "the disallowed edit did not succeed but was recorded"
  -> REJECTED: no-observed-outcome reason (exit 1). No signal word in the
     paragraph, caught by mechanism (b).
- "the error never showed up"
  -> ACCEPTED as an observation. Failure is only the standing NOT PERFORMED
     count (exit 1). RESIDUAL P2: SIGNAL_RE's word "error" is the noun of the
     thing that never appeared; DENIAL_RE does not catch mid-sentence "never".

Root cause of P1/P2: mechanism (b) is a keyword list too; signal words can
name the thing that was NOT observed, so a denial that mentions "failure"/"error"
can still pass. This matches the check's own stance (both mechanisms judge
shapes only; semantic genuineness remains the independent verifier's read).
Reported for the record; no fix requested or applied.

